# Operator contamination ledger — MACHINE-RECIPROCITY-1.
#
# The readership store keeps an hour, not a timestamp, so a request the
# operator made at 01:12 and a visitor's at 01:58 land in the same cell. Both
# arrive as `curl`. Nothing in the data separates them afterwards, so they are
# counted here at the moment they are made.
#
# Retrospective, for arm 1: two prechecks ran before the visitor was
# dispatched, at 01:12:14Z (refused, stale revision) and 01:14:20Z (passed).
# Each is 2 requests to /llms.txt and 1 to /api/machines/ask, which accounts
# for exactly the 4 and 2 the server recorded in hour 496969 — and the
# transcript independently shows the visitor never reached the site at all.
llms.txt 4 /api/machines/ask 2 2026-09-11T01:14:20Z precheck
llms.txt 2 /api/machines/ask 1 2026-09-11T01:20:47Z precheck
# Retrospective: the observer ran 3 times before it logged itself — once while
# being built (~01:10Z) and once for each of arms 1 and 2. Three requests to
# /api/readership in hour 496969 are therefore the operator's, which with the
# visitor's own fetch of it accounts for the 5 recorded.
/api/readership 3 2026-09-11T01:22:00Z observer
/api/readership 1 2026-09-11T01:28:02.633Z observer
